WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.330
Hi. I'm Gus Halwani.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.610
I've followed one thread
for most of my life.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.430
It started with sound.

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.450
I trained as a sound engineer.

5
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.200
Then I got curious about what
the brain does with sound,

6
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.670
so I went to MIT and did my
doctorate in neuroscience.

7
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.250
I used brain imaging —
MRI, DTI and fMRI —

8
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.700
to study how musicians' brains
differ from non-musicians',

9
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.950
and what that could mean
for recovery after a stroke.

10
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.730
After that, I started building things.

11
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.240
I founded NeuRace, which read
race car drivers' brain and

12
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.370
body signals live on track.

13
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.280
I co-founded a startup
that makes visual stories

14
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.810
for neurodivergent kids
and their families.

15
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.890
And I was Chief Innovation Officer
at The Possible Zone, in Boston.

16
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.830
So what do I do now? Two things.

17
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.810
One: creative work.

18
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:55.970
I develop ideas, and I make images,
film, sound, and interactive work.

19
00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.870
Two: technology, and change.

20
00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.470
I help organizations choose new
technology and actually use it.

21
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.610
Sometimes that's designing a product.

22
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.630
Sometimes it's leading the build.

23
00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.930
Sometimes it's helping a
team change how it works.

24
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.370
I take on select speaking engagements,
workshops, and project work.

25
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.510
If you're working on something at that
edge of creativity and technology,

26
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.090
let's set up a jam session.

27
00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:22.970
I'd like to hear what
you're working on.
